  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 5.1% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $14.90B (5.1% lower over 30D) hints that tokenized asset growth paused or reversed\u2014more consistent with risk-off allocation or redemptions than a pure news cycle. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/14/former-ftx-europe-chief-targets-u-s-stock-tokenization-with-new-sec-exemption\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Former FTX Europe chief targets U.S. tokenized stock trading with new SEC exemption</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/13/bny-citadel-securities-test-tokenized-u-s-treasuries-to-speed-up-wall-street-financing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BNY, Citadel Securities test tokenized U.S. Treasuries to speed up Wall Street financing</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/10/14/dutch-regulator-approves-qivalis-as-electronic-money-institution-under-mica-rules\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dutch central bank grants Qivalis e-money license for MiCA-compliant euro token</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/10/13/largest-philippines-crypto-exchange-coins-ph-said-to-face-central-bank-regulatory-action\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Largest Philippines crypto exchange, Coins.ph, said to face central bank regulatory action</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
